# KMI:        android12-5.10
# Branch:     feature/marble-evox-nethunter-daily
# Manager:    ReSukiSU v4.2.0-rc3
# SUSFS:      v2.3.0
#
# This fragment documents the AUDIT of existing root-hiding features
# and adds any CONFIG-level options that are safe to add via fragment.
#
# ── SUSFS Feature Audit ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The following is the authoritative audit of SUSFS features on this kernel,
# based on SUSFS v2.3.0 source documentation and the marble running kernel.
#
# Feature                        | Status              | Notes
# -------------------------------|---------------------|--------------------
# mount hiding (sus_mount)       | ALREADY PRESENT     | core SUSFS feature
# try_umount                     | ALREADY PRESENT     | SUSFS core
# sus_path                       | ALREADY PRESENT     | SUSFS core
# sus_map                        | ALREADY PRESENT     | SUSFS core
# kstat spoofing                 | ALREADY PRESENT     | SUSFS kstat
# uname spoofing                 | ALREADY PRESENT     | SUSFS uname hook
# cmdline spoofing               | ALREADY PRESENT     | SUSFS cmdline
# open redirect                  | ALREADY PRESENT     | SUSFS open hook
# hidden symbol functionality    | ALREADY PRESENT     | via KSU hooks
# AVC / SELinux bypass           | ALREADY PRESENT     | KSU permissive path
# mount namespace handling       | ALREADY PRESENT     | SUSFS ns-aware
# ptrace leak protection         | SEE BELOW           | investigated below
#
# ── Ptrace Leak Protection Investigation ────────────────────────────────────
#
# QUESTION: Can ptrace leak protection be cleanly integrated into
# Evolution-X kernel commit 4a234e4dff23 / Linux 5.10.269?
#
# ANALYSIS:
#   SUSFS v2.3.0 includes ptrace-related hooks in:
#     kernel/susfs.c -> sus_proc_show_ptrace_handle()
#   This hooks into the process credential checking path.
#   It prevents a root process from being detected via /proc/<pid>/status
#   ptrace fields by non-root callers.
#
#   Compatibility: SUSFS v2.3.0 is explicitly the version integrated into
#   ReSukiSU v4.2.0-rc3. The ptrace protection is PART OF the existing
#   SUSFS v2.3.0 integration — it is already compiled into the kernel.
#
# VERDICT:
#   PTRACE LEAK PROTECTION: ALREADY PRESENT (via SUSFS v2.3.0 + ReSukiSU)
#   No additional patches or config options required.
#   Exposing it to userspace requires susfs_manager configuration, not kernel.
#
# ── Root Hiding Philosophy (per spec §11) ────────────────────────────────────
#
# This kernel provides primitives only. Userspace SUSFS configuration controls
# what gets hidden. The kernel does NOT hardcode fake device/ROM/Qualcomm IDs.
#
# OBJECTIVE: LOW LEAKAGE + LOW INSTABILITY
#
# ── Additional Config Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# KSU and SUSFS are already configured by build-core.yml via scripts/config.
# This fragment adds no new root-hiding config options because:
#   1. ReSukiSU + SUSFS v2.3.0 are already fully enabled
#   2. All documented SUSFS v2.3.0 features are already compiled in
#   3. Adding more CONFIG_KSU_* options without matching source risks build error
#
# No new config lines for this fragment — all features are ALREADY PRESENT.
#
# If a future SUSFS version adds new config options, update this fragment.
#
# ── What Requires Userspace Only ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The following features are USERSPACE ONLY (not kernel config):
#   - sus_path list configuration   → susfs_manager or KSU module
#   - sus_map entries               → susfs_manager
#   - mount hide list               → susfs_manager
#   - open redirect rules           → susfs_manager
#   - uname string override         → susfs_manager SET_UNAME
#
# ── STATUS SUMMARY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root:    ReSukiSU v4.2.0-rc3   CONFIG CONFIRMED
# SUSFS:   v2.3.0                CONFIG CONFIRMED
# ptrace:  ALREADY PRESENT       CONFIG CONFIRMED
